name: "🤖 Copilot Task"
description: "Assign a well-scoped implementation task to GitHub Copilot coding agent."
title: "[Task] "
labels: ["copilot-task"]
assignees: []
body:
  - type: markdown
    attributes:
      value: |
        Use this template to create a task for GitHub Copilot coding agent.
        
        **Tips for better results:**
        - Be specific about what needs to change and why
        - List acceptance criteria clearly — Copilot treats these as a checklist
        - Name specific files or directories when you know which ones need changing
        - Keep the scope to one coherent feature or fix per issue

  - type: textarea
    id: description
    attributes:
      label: "What needs to be done?"
      description: "Clear description of the work required. Write this as if it were a prompt — because it is."
      placeholder: |
        {{TASK_DESCRIPTION_PLACEHOLDER}}
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: textarea
    id: acceptance-criteria
    attributes:
      label: "Acceptance Criteria"
      description: "What does done look like? List specific, testable requirements."
      placeholder: |
        - [ ] Feature works as described
        - [ ] Unit tests cover the new logic
        - [ ] `{{AGENT_VERIFY_COMMAND}}` passes with zero errors
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: textarea
    id: files
    attributes:
      label: "Files to Create or Change"
      description: "List the files you expect to be created or modified. Leave blank if unsure."
    validations:
      required: false

  - type: textarea
    id: context
    attributes:
      label: "Additional Context"
      description: "Any constraints, references, or background that will help Copilot understand the task."
    validations:
      required: false
